WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.780
And we know this has created a lot of hardship for so many.

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:05.613
This is trash.

00:00:05.613 --> 00:00:08.400
It's crippling a sector of our economy,

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.780
that's already limping.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.260
To persecute us

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.950
as an industry based on five or six weeks

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:17.460
of spiking cases that probably have very little to do

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:21.230
with outdoor dining is just crazy.

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:22.470
On November 22nd,

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.980
Los Angeles became the only county in America

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:27.390
to ban outdoor dining this winter

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:29.090
for a minimum three weeks.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:30.730
This order could put out of business

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:34.150
many California restaurants that were barely hanging on.

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:36.580
Some of which recently invested in retrofitting

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:38.750
for exclusively outdoor dining.

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:40.730
The worst part, according to critics

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:43.360
is that the public health agency issuing the order

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:49.000
has provided no concrete evidence that outdoor dining is a significant source of COVID spread.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.500
I personally feel like we're being punished.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.680
Kat Turner is a chef and partner at Highly Likely cafe

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:57.140
in the West Adams neighborhood of Los Angeles.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:58.930
The data to support that

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:00.830
COVID is being spread through outdoor dining,

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:02.539
I think it's extremely flimsy.

00:01:02.539 --> 00:01:05.940
I just don't understand the agenda that's being pushed.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:09.590
They've shut us without saying, hey, here's a solution,

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:11.280
this is how we're gonna help businesses,

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:13.010
this is how we're gonna help you get through this period,

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:14.220
because they knew it was coming,

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.610
but where's the planning?

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:16.900
Where's the foresight?

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:20.030
David Combes is the CEO of Botanical Group

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:22.530
which owns two restaurants in West Hollywood

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.400
including EP and LP,

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:28.010
which shifted all of its business to outdoor rooftop dining.

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:30.900
We've spent a considerable amount of money,

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:32.420
our additional investments

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:34.300
being in the hundreds of thousands of dollars

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.620
from additional staffing required,

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:39.590
security required to manage patrons

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:42.010
and make sure there's distancing applied barriers

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:43.808
and sanitizers.

00:01:43.808 --> 00:01:46.820
Health Department--they visit us to check for compliance.

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:48.790
I'm happy to say that we've sailed through

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:49.760
with flying colors,

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:52.130
certainly made our life challenging

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:54.460
and profitability an impossibility.

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:56.410
LA county's Department of Public Health

00:01:56.410 --> 00:01:58.820
issued the order the weekend before Thanksgiving.

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:01.730
Pointing to a 108% increase in case numbers

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:03.490
and rising hospitalizations

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:06.230
as rationale for the renewed restrictions.

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:08.370
Gathering with people you do not live with

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:12.680
can increase the chances of getting or spreading COVID19.

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:13.940
LA Public Health Director.

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:16.170
Barbara Ferrer held an online press conference

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:18.220
on November 23rd to discuss the order

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:20.460
and estimates from the county's contact tracing

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:23.730
that 10 to 15% of COVID transmissions are linked

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:25.630
to dining experiences.

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:26.920
Though she hasn't clarified,

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:28.690
how many of those transmissions

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:31.810
were attributed to outdoor dining at restaurants

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:33.930
and declined to provide the underlying data

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:35.530
when pressed by reporters.

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:38.160
Has there been a noted outbreak

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:41.930
that has come from people dining outside?

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:43.190
People are eating and drinking

00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:45.330
and they're not wearing their face coverings

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:47.990
for the vast majority of time that they're there.

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:49.350
When they're gathered with people

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:51.280
who are not in their household,

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:52.700
there just ends up being

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:55.080
a significant amount of risk associated.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:58.160
I think the question, and I don't know that you answered it,

00:02:58.160 --> 00:02:59.890
is she wanted to know a number

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:02.800
of outbreaks as a result of restaurants--

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:05.845
I don't have those numbers in front of me

00:03:05.845 --> 00:03:08.460
but I will be happy to

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:10.260
work with our communications team

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:11.370
and we'll get those numbers.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:15.033
The Health Department didn't respond to Reason's follow up requests for those numbers,

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:16.840
and the county's online data portal

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:20.200
identifies only 16 restaurants as outbreak sites.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:23.590
Most of them fast food restaurants involving only employees

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:24.920
not outdoor diners.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:29.230
And restaurants don't make the county's top five list of COVID exposure sites.

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:30.300
The counties also found

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:31.960
that the vast majority of restaurants

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:33.520
do comply with its health orders

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.320
and that cases fell through the summer,

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:37.530
even as outdoor dining was allowed.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:40.810
Given that you haven't identified an actual

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:43.820
source of an outbreak being in outdoor dining

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:46.750
how do you rationalize the closure

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:49.050
and how do you expect

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:53.150
to measure whether it actually is accomplishing

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:54.690
what you're hoping to accomplish?

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:58.360
We know that places where people are gathering

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:00.370
without wearing their face coverings

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:05.080
are places where transmission is easiest and most likely.

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:08.450
But we will, as always, watch our data.

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:11.190
The counties had eight months to get their shit together

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:13.780
in relation to contact, tracing, and also testing.

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:15.820
So it feels like we are being disadvantaged

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:18.200
by a lack of process from the LA County.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.680
And now, for political optics,

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:23.160
it's, the requirement for them to do something is

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:24.130
well the first thing we're gonna do is

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.760
we're gonna shut down restaurants and bars.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:27.090
I think it's stupid.

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:29.380
I think people are still gonna wanna get together,

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:30.990
and now they're gonna do it inside

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:32.290
at other people's homes,

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:35.252
instead of meeting outside at a restaurant to have dinner.

00:04:35.252 --> 00:04:36.890
And now that it's colder outside

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:38.340
they're not gonna wanna sit in the backyard.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:39.740
They're gonna sit in the living room.

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:42.010
The Los Angeles County Board of supervisors

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.750
voted three to two to uphold the Health Department's order.

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:47.870
One restaurant owner has already filed suit against the County.

00:04:47.870 --> 00:04:50.710
Turner says she worries about the unintended consequences

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:54.210
of an indefinite shutdown of one of the only relatively

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:57.600
safe places that people in Los Angeles can gather.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:01.090
With the very fabric of our mental health

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:03.840
as a community kind of hanging in the wires,

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:06.170
and the financial stability of us as a business

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:07.870
and the livelihood,

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:10.800
the literal survival of my team gets completely

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:13.504
irresponsible to shut down outdoor dining.

00:05:13.504 --> 00:05:17.210
Like what we have here is good for the community

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:19.070
and it's good for the economy

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:20.170
and it's good for our staff

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:21.370
and we're doing it safely.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:24.555
Like this is not dangerous.

